hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16116","Abdullah narrated to us, Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said ibn Khalid al-Qarazi, from Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili, that he said: I saw Abu Lahab at Ukaz following the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O people, this has gone astray, so let him not lead you astray from the gods of your fathers. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flees from him while he is on his heels, and we follow him, and we were youths, as though I am looking at him, cross-eyed, with two locks of hair, the whitest of people and the most handsome of them."
"16117","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Rabiah ibn Abbad, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhu al-Majaz calling the people, and behind him a cross-eyed man saying: Let not this turn you away from the religion of your gods. I said: Who is this? They said: This is his uncle Abu Lahab."
"16118","Abdullah narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Rabiah ibn Abbad, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling the people to Islam at Dhu al-Majaz, and behind him a cross-eyed man saying: Let not this overcome you against your religion and the religion of your fathers. I said to my father, and I was a boy: Who is this cross-eyed one walking behind him? He said: This is his uncle Abu Lahab. Abbad said: I think between Muhammad ibn Amr and Rabiah is Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir."
"16119","Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Sulayman al-Dabbi Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Musayyibi narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili, and he was a Jahili who became Muslim, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my own sight at the market of Dhu al-Majaz saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper. And he enters its paths, and the people crowd over him, and I did not see anyone saying anything, while he does not fall silent, saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper, except that behind him was a cross-eyed man, bright-faced, with two locks, saying: He is an apostate liar. So I said: Who is this? They said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah, and he mentions prophethood. I said: Who is this who belies him? They said: His uncle Abu Lahab. I said: You were then small. He said: No, by Allah, I was then discerning."
"16120","Abdullah narrated to us, Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salamah, meaning Ibn Abi al-Husam, narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us that he heard Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) going around to the people at Mina in their dwellings before he emigrated to Madinah, saying: O people, Allah Almighty commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him. He said: And behind him a man saying: This commands you to abandon the religion of your fathers. So I asked: Who is this man? It was said: This is Abu Lahab."
"16121","Abdullah narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said, Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydillah ibn al-Abbas narrated to me, he said: I heard Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili say: I was with my father, a young man, looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) following the tribes, and behind him a cross-eyed bright man with a thick lock. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stands over a tribe and says: O sons of so-and-so, I am the Messenger of Allah to you; I command you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and to believe me until I carry out from Allah what He sent me with. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finishes his speech, the other says from behind him: O sons of so-and-so, this wants from you to cast off al-Lat and al-Uzza and your allies of the clan of Banu Malik ibn Uqaysh, to what he brought of innovation and error. So do not listen to him nor follow him. So I said to my father: Who is this? He said: His uncle Abu Lahab."
"16122","Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from his father Abu al-Zinad, he said: I saw a man called Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dili, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passing in the paths of Dhu al-Majaz, except that they follow him, and they said: This is Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib. He said: And a cross-eyed bright-faced man with two locks follows him in the paths of Dhu al-Majaz, saying: He is an apostate liar. So I said: Who is this? They said: This is his uncle Abu Lahab."
"16123","Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Husayn ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Duali and from one who narrated to him, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Rabiah ibn Abbad, he said: By Allah, I remember him going around the dwellings at Mina, and I was with my father, a young boy, and behind him a handsome cross-eyed man with two locks. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over a people he said: I am the Messenger of Allah; He commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him. And the one behind him says: This calls you to leave the religion of your fathers and to cast off al-Lat and al-Uzza and your allies of Banu Malik ibn Uqaysh, to what he brought of innovation and error. He said: So I said to my father: Who is this? He said: This is his uncle Abu Lahab Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
